Production of Large Volume Organic Chemicals, BREF LVOC (@ic-large-organics: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_78ET6A4D7AX8HPQTYAMZMAG16B
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Production of Large Volume Organic Chemicals, BREF LVOC. December 2017. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/production-large-volume-organic-chemicals-0).

The fourteen-chapter technical book joins generic continuous-process principles with major illustrative petrochemical and oxygenated, nitrogenated and halogenated product systems.

Read the whole general/process treatment and complete relevant cases, including lower olefins, aromatics, ethylbenzene/styrene, formaldehyde, ethylene oxide/glycols, phenol, ethanolamines, isocyanates, EDC/VCM and hydrogen peroxide. Preserve full reaction/separation and resource/residual boundaries rather than extracting one favorable performance number.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled. JRC109279, DOI 10.2760/77304. Its reuse statement permits attributed, undistorted reuse subject to third-party rights; this does not make every component CC licensed.

